{
 "id": "P05",
 "kind": "echarts",
 "title": "Haiku at xhigh keeps up with Sonnet from 2% up, not below",
 "section": "results",
 "order": 60,
 "caption": "Top: share of backdoors caught as the audit budget grows, with 95% bands; Haiku at its default is there for reference. Bottom: Sonnet's lead over Haiku xhigh. Its band comes from a paired bootstrap, so it is tighter than comparing the top bands by eye.",
 "notes": [
  "This changes the web/ summary page, which says the two can't be separated because their intervals overlap. With exact budgets and a paired test the gap is small but above zero at every budget, and Marnick's matched-rate test agrees.",
  "Method, as agreed: Marnick's matched-rate number for the tight-budget claim, this exact-budget curve for the overview. Check the gap is quoted the way results/analysis/MONITOR-GAP.md means it.",
  "Below 1% the cutoff rests on 5 honest programs or fewer, so the bands are wide. The gap there is real but its size is not well measured."
 ],
